# Docker build context exclusions.
#
# The first block is a SECURITY CONTROL, not an optimisation.
#
# artifacts/api-server/.env holds live third-party credentials (an SMTP app
# password and an SMS provider account token). A build context copies everything
# it is not told to exclude, and anything copied into a stage can end up in an
# image layer that outlives the build. Never remove these lines. Compose hands
# the containers their env at runtime through env_file instead.
#
#   See specs/001-docker-compose-stack/research.md § Security finding
#   Verified by  specs/001-docker-compose-stack/quickstart.md V13
#
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Dependencies — reinstalled inside the image from the frozen lockfile
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build outputs — rebuilt inside the image, and stale copies would silently win
**/dist
**/build
**/.turbo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Generated release bundles (node deploy/make-release.mjs)
release

# Version control and editor/agent state
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.vscode
.idea
.claude
.agents
.cursor
.config

# Spec Kit working files — not needed to build or run anything
specs
.specify

# Docs
docs
*.md
!deploy/db/**

# Replit local state
.cache
.local

# Noise
**/*.log
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
**/*.swp
**/coverage
